487
00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:56.790
you know, you taking the heat like that around them and having that nice little moment.
你知道的，你替他们背锅，和他们有了那个温馨的小时刻。

488
00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:59.310
I think that that to me felt more right.
我觉得对我来说，那样感觉更对味。

489
00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:01.190
And I love that we ended up going there with the story.
我很高兴我们最终让故事走向了那个方向。

490
00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:04.870
Yeah, it was going to be a whole Halloween episode.
对，原本打算拍成一整集万圣节特辑的。

491
00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.130
And then they changed it up.
然后他们改了主意。

492
00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:06.810
Yes.
是的。

493
00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:11.390
Anthony shared in the DVD that all those Halloween costumes would actually be distracting
安东尼在DVD里分享说，所有的这些万圣节戏服其实会分散观众对

494
00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:12.830
from all the other storylines.
其他所有剧情线的注意力。

495
00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:14.590
So they just made it the cold open.
所以他们才决定只改成片头短剧。

496
00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:17.030
And I have a costume breakdown.
我有一份戏服详细解析。

497
00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:17.750
Oh, good.
哦，太好了。

498
00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:20.110
Because I have some good details about some of the costumes.
因为我掌握了一些关于某些戏服的精彩细节。

499
00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:20.550
Okay.
好的。

500
00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:21.930
What's everyone wearing, Angela?
大家都穿了什么呢，安吉拉？

501
00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:24.670
So we have the scripts thanks to Jamesopedia.
所以多亏了詹姆斯百科，我们拿到了剧本。

502
00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:27.570
So per the script, here are some details.
根据剧本，这里有一些细节。

503
00:19:28.170 --> 00:19:33.270
Stanley, in the script it says, is wearing a creature from the Black Lagoon rubber mask
剧本上说，斯坦利穿着一件《黑湖妖潭》的橡胶面具

504
00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.110
with his regular suit.
搭配他平常的西装。

505
00:19:35.510 --> 00:19:35.650
Okay.
好的。

506
00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:40.230
Creed, per the script, is an amazing Joker from Batman.
根据剧本，克里德是一个超棒的蝙蝠侠里的小丑。

507
00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:44.270
Whereas Kevin is a, quote, lame Joker.
而凯文则是一个，引号里的，很逊的小丑。

508
00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:48.550
And in the script it says, Dwight is also a Joker.
剧本里还写着，德怀特也是一个小丑。

509
00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:51.430
Kelly is Carrie Bradshaw from Sex and the City.
凯莉打扮成《欲望都市》里的凯莉·布拉德肖。

510
00:19:51.610 --> 00:19:54.010
Ryan is Gordon Gekko from Wall Street.
瑞恩打扮成《华尔街》里的戈登·盖柯。

511
00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:55.690
Very fitting for Ryan.
非常适合瑞恩。

512
00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:57.790
Oscar is Uncle Sam.
奥斯卡是山姆大叔。

513
00:19:58.010 --> 00:19:59.170
Meredith, a cheerleader.
梅雷迪思是拉拉队员。

514
00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:00.990
Phyllis is Raggedy Ann.
菲利斯是安妮贝尔娃娃。

515
00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:06.870
Andy, per the script, it says, he's dressed as a cat with whiskers on his face.
根据剧本，安迪打扮成一只猫，脸上画着胡须。

516
00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:09.610
Angela has brought back her cat costume.
安杰拉又穿回了她的猫咪服装。

517
00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:09.930
Yes.
没错。

518
00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:10.810
Always a classic.
永远的经典。

519
00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:14.610
And Jim is just wearing a name tag that says Dave.
而吉姆只是戴着一个写着“戴夫”的名牌。

520
00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:20.730
And of course, Pam, the solo Halloween costume wearer at corporate is dressed as Charlie Chaplin.
当然，帕姆，公司里唯一穿万圣节服装的人，打扮成了查理·卓别林。

521
00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:21.310
Yes.
是的。

522
00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:24.810
I reached out to our wardrobe designer, Alicia Raycraft.
我联系了我们的服装设计艾丽西亚·雷克拉夫特。

523
00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:25.730
Oh, great.
哦，太好了。

524
00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:30.470
So, starting this season, Alicia took over for Carrie Bennett.
从这季开始，艾丽西亚接替了凯莉·贝内特。

525
00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:36.190
Alicia was amazing, particularly, I think, at building wardrobe from scratch.
艾丽西亚非常厉害，尤其是我觉得她在从零开始制作服装方面。

526
00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:41.150
My memories of her when I would visit her in the wardrobe trailer were that she always had,
我对她的记忆是，当我去看望服装车里的她时，她总是带着

527
00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:46.870
like, one of those fabric mannequins with, like, swatches on it, pinned on it, or on her wall.
那种布料人体模型，上面别着布料小样，或者挂在墙上。

528
00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:49.910
I am telling you, she was always pinning something to something.
我跟你说，她总是在把什么东西别在什么东西上。

529
00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:50.230
Yes.
是的。

530
00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:52.110
And then standing back and looking at it.
然后退后一步看着它。

531
00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:52.270
Yeah.
对。

532
00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:54.350
And then moving a swatch here, up and down.
然后把一个小样移到这儿，上下移动。

533
00:20:54.570 --> 00:21:01.670
She said that with this episode, she had to really ride the line of designing wardrobe,
她说在这集里，她必须很好地把握平衡，既要设计服装，

534
00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:06.650
but also making sure that the costumes looked like things that we could have put together ourselves.
又要确保这些服装看起来像是我们自己能拼凑出来的东西。

535
00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:07.210
Right.
没错。

536
00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:11.850
The idea is that if Kevin is going to dress like the Joker, it'd be Kevin's effort.
这个想法是，如果凯文要打扮成小丑，那得是凯文的努力。

537
00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:14.010
It'd be, like, something Kevin had to put together.
应该像是凯文自己拼凑出来的东西。

538
00:21:14.010 --> 00:21:14.550
Yes.
是的。

539
00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:20.130
Like you said, the script said that Creed's Joker was supposed to be the best version of the Joker.
就像你说的，剧本上说克里德的小丑应该是最好版本的小丑。

540
00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:21.790
Kevin's was supposed to be lame.
凯文的则应该是很逊的。

541
00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:23.310
And they're the Dark Knight Joker.
而且他们都是《黑暗骑士》里的小丑。

542
00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:23.970
Yes.
是的。

543
00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:25.370
That's what Alicia said.
艾丽西亚是这么说的。

544
00:21:25.490 --> 00:21:29.290
They were supposed to be based on the Heath Ledger Joker.
它们本该是以希斯·莱杰的小丑为原型的。

545
00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:34.910
And so, she had a picture, and she made a shopping list, and she still had her shopping liSt.
所以，她有一张照片，列了一张购物清单，她现在还保留着那张购物清单。

546
00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:35.650
Stop it.
别开玩笑了。

547
00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:36.770
I love her.
我太爱她了。

548
00:21:36.950 --> 00:21:38.050
This is what it said.
上面是这么写的。

549
00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:45.330
They had to go shop for a vest with a high neck center front, green for Creed, not for Kevin.
他们得去买一件前门襟高领的马背心，克里德的是绿色，凯文的不是。

550
00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.310
Because Creed got it right, and Kevin didn't.
因为克里德买对了，而凯文没有。

551
00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:48.830
Correct.
没错。

552
00:21:49.190 --> 00:21:57.750
They needed a gray or dark lilac patterned shirt, green or olive tie with a pattern, pinstripe navy
他们需要一件灰色或深丁香紫有纹理的衬衫、一条有图案的绿色或橄榄绿色领带、细条纹海军蓝

553
00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:05.870
pants, pleated for Kevin, but flat front for Creed, argyle socks, black Oxford shoes for Creed,
裤子，凯文穿打褶的，而克里德穿平腰的，菱形格袜子，克里德穿黑色牛津鞋，

554
00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:08.870
but Kevin is to wear his regular character shoes.
但凯文要穿他平时角色的鞋子。

555
00:22:09.630 --> 00:22:17.050
She said the overall direction in shopping for Kevin was that all of the clothes they purchased should look like they came from his closet.
她说为凯文采购的总体指导方针是，他们购买的所有衣服看起来都应该像是从他自己的衣橱里拿出来的。

556
00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:22.630
And the direction for Creed was that Creed went out and picked it out specifically for Halloween.
而对克里德的要求则是，克里德是专门为万圣节出去挑选的。

557
00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:23.230
Yeah.
对。

558
00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:29.090
But for Dwight, she said they went with a nod to the Jack Nicholson version of the Joker.
但对于德怀特，她说他们借鉴了杰克·尼克松版本的Joker（小丑）。

559
00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:35.770
I thought something was different when I rewatched it because the way they drew the smile did not look like the Heath Ledger Joker.
当我重温时，我发现有些地方不一样，因为他们画的微笑看起来不像希斯·莱杰的小丑。

560
00:22:35.770 --> 00:22:41.330
That's how they were like, how do we do three Jokers, but it's not all the same costume or the same look.
这就是他们当时的设想，我们该如何呈现三个不同的小丑，但又不是全都是相同的服装或造型。

561
00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:49.950
But she also shared with me that she brought in a rack of clothes and that Rain really put together his costume from everything she had bought,
但她也跟我分享说，她拿来了一排衣服，雷恩确实用她买的所有东西自己拼凑出了他的服装，

562
00:22:50.170 --> 00:22:52.610
which tracks with when we talked to Carrie.
这和我们与凯莉交谈时的情况吻合。

563
00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:57.170
And Carrie Bennett said that Rain was always really invested in what his character wore.
凯莉·贝内特说过，雷恩总是对他的角色穿什么非常上心。

564
00:22:57.370 --> 00:22:58.210
That's awesome.
太棒了。

565
00:22:58.450 --> 00:22:59.150
So let's see.
那么我们来看看。

566
00:22:59.250 --> 00:22:59.830
What's next?
接下来是什么？

567
00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:03.150
We got a lot of questions about Andy's kitten costume.
我们收到了很多关于安迪小猫服装的问题。

568
00:23:03.390 --> 00:23:03.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

569
00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:10.430
A lot of people wrote in to say they thought it looked a little bit like, my favorite was Katie L said,
很多人写信来说，他们觉得这看起来有点像，我最喜欢的是凯蒂·L说的，

570
00:23:10.550 --> 00:23:14.810
it looks like an off-brand Rum Tum Tugger costume from the musical Cats.
这看起来像音乐剧《猫》里山寨版的拉姆·谭·塔格（Rum Tum Tugger）服装。

571
00:23:15.150 --> 00:23:20.530
She said, in my mind, I like to think Andy was in a school production of Cats and he still had his costume.
她说，在我的脑海里，我愿意相信安迪曾参演过学校制作的《猫》，并且他至今还留着他的戏服。

572
00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.070
Katie L, you would be right on there.
凯蒂·L，你可真是说对了。

573
00:23:24.490 --> 00:23:30.410
Dave told me that Greg was very involved in Ed's costume.
戴夫告诉我，格雷格对埃德的服装参与度很高。

574
00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:31.110
Really?
真的吗？

575
00:23:31.110 --> 00:23:38.630
Yes, that he wanted it to look like it was from the musical Cats, and he went over the top to please Angela.
是的，他希望这看起来像是来自音乐剧《猫》，而且他不遗余力地想要取悦安吉拉。

576
00:23:38.890 --> 00:23:39.270
Right.
没错。

577
00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:41.990
He was not just going to draw whiskers on his face, guys.
伙计们，他可不只是在脸上画几根胡须那么简单。

578
00:23:42.590 --> 00:23:48.790
Alicia said she showed Greg a bunch of photos from the Broadway musical of Cats, and Greg picked his favorites,
艾丽西亚说她给格雷格看了一堆百老汇音乐剧《猫》的照片，格雷格挑出了他最喜欢的，

579
00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:51.870
but she did not base this cat on any one character.
但她并没有以任何单一角色为原型来设计这只猫。

580
00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:52.890
It was a meld.
这是一个融合体。

581
00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:53.430
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

582
00:23:53.670 --> 00:23:55.690
She built that whole costume from scratch.
她从零开始制作了整套服装。

583
00:23:55.970 --> 00:23:58.570
She bought a unitard and hand-painted it.
她买了一件紧身衣并亲手绘制。

584
00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:00.630
She used to do textile painting.
她以前是做纺织品彩绘的。

585
00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:01.110
Wow.
哇。

586
00:24:01.110 --> 00:24:02.430
I mean, that's amazing.
我是说，这太厉害了。

587
00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:06.070
And then she found another email that she shared with me.
然后她找到了另一封与我分享的邮件。

588
00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:14.510
It was an email to her crew detailing how to build the little, like, fur diaper thing that he's wearing.
那是发给她团队的一封邮件，详细说明了如何制作他穿的那个小小的、类似毛绒尿布的东西。

589
00:24:14.650 --> 00:24:15.930
What is it, right?
那到底是什么，对吧？

590
00:24:16.290 --> 00:24:17.110
Yeah, I don't know.
对，我不知道。

591
00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:22.530
It looks like fur underwear, and then there's also, like, a rope belt and a tail, and oh, my goodness.
它看起来像毛绒内裤，然后还有一条绳子腰带和一个尾巴，哦，天哪。

592
00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:23.170
Yes.
是的。

593
00:24:23.410 --> 00:24:29.230
She said, please make a loincloth using a thong or small brief underwear as a base,
她说，请以丁字裤或小号三角内裤为基础制作一个遮阴布，

594
00:24:29.250 --> 00:24:36.010
and then swatch Phelps wool crepe and heavy knits on top, and please get faux fur for some gloves.
然后在上面拼接菲尔普斯羊毛呢和重磅针织面料，请再准备一些用于手套的人造毛皮。

595
00:24:38.930 --> 00:24:39.750
So amazing.
太惊艳了。

596
00:24:39.970 --> 00:24:45.190
So that is how she put together all of those costumes, which were really amazing.
这就是她拼凑出所有这些服装的过程，它们真的太棒了。

597
00:24:45.350 --> 00:24:46.570
And I remember my costume.
而且我还记得我的戏服。

598
00:24:46.790 --> 00:24:50.870
We did, like, Pam went to a store and rented a tux, basically.
我们当时做的是，潘基本上是去店里租了一套燕尾服。

599
00:24:51.210 --> 00:24:52.990
Well, I took a lot of photos this day.
好吧，我这天拍了很多照片。

600
00:24:53.150 --> 00:24:54.850
I have some great ones of you and Rain.
我有一些你和雷恩的很棒的照片。

601
00:24:55.050 --> 00:24:56.630
You guys were hanging out by your trailer.
你们当时在你们的拖车附近闲逛。

602
00:24:56.830 --> 00:24:59.710
I was walking by you guys in my cat costume,
我穿着猫咪服装从你们旁边走过，

603
00:24:59.710 --> 00:25:06.050
and I see Rain as the Joker talking to Jenna as Charlie Chaplin, just casually hanging out.
然后我看到雷恩扮演的小丑和扮演查理·卓别林的珍娜在聊天，就那样随性地呆在一起。

604
00:25:06.510 --> 00:25:08.010
And so I took pictures.
于是我拍了照片。

605
00:25:08.230 --> 00:25:09.190
They're some of my favorite.
它们是我最喜欢的照片之一。

606
00:25:09.490 --> 00:25:11.230
Well, I think he put that one in his book.
嗯，我想他把那张照片放进他的书里了。

607
00:25:11.410 --> 00:25:12.310
I gave it to him.
我送给他的。

608
00:25:12.350 --> 00:25:12.570
Yeah.
对。

609
00:25:12.670 --> 00:25:13.270
That's from me.
那是我的。

610
00:25:13.390 --> 00:25:18.390
I loved this episode, Angela, because I had been away for a very long time at Pratt,
我特别喜欢这一集，安吉拉，因为我在普瑞特艺术学院离开很久了，

611
00:25:18.750 --> 00:25:22.850
but, you know, the corporate offices were over on the warehouse set.
但是，你知道的，公司办公室是在仓库片场那边。

612
00:25:22.950 --> 00:25:23.990
We never got to see you.
我们从来没机会见到你。

613
00:25:24.110 --> 00:25:25.510
But you did on this day.
但这一天你见到了。

614
00:25:25.750 --> 00:25:26.190
Exactly.
没错。

615
00:25:26.190 --> 00:25:31.790
And I got to participate in the Halloween, which was always one of my favorite things on our show.
而且我能参与万圣节活动，这一直是我们剧中最让我喜爱的事情之一。

616
00:25:32.130 --> 00:25:35.830
And I would have been really bummed if I didn't get to see everybody in their costumes.
如果没能见到大家穿着各自的服装，我真的会觉得很沮丧。

617
00:25:35.830 --> 00:25:37.470
But I got to be in hair makeup.
但我去了发型化妆间。

618
00:25:37.690 --> 00:25:39.270
And we were in there a long time.
我们在里面待了很长时间。

619
00:25:39.430 --> 00:25:40.390
Me, not so long.
我嘛，没那么久。

620
00:25:40.470 --> 00:25:42.610
But, oh, my gosh, Ed had to come in really early.
但是，天哪，埃德必须来得非常早。

621
00:25:42.750 --> 00:25:43.030
Yeah.
对。

622
00:25:43.330 --> 00:25:44.450
And so did Phyllis.
菲利斯也是。

623
00:25:44.610 --> 00:25:45.990
Like, there was a lot of makeup there.
就像是，那里有很多妆要化。

624
00:25:46.190 --> 00:25:49.090
Well, my hair was not easy to wash out, I'll tell you that.
嗯，我的头发可不好洗干净，我跟你说。

625
00:25:49.310 --> 00:25:50.190
Are your eyebrows.
还有你的眉毛。

626
00:25:50.190 --> 00:25:52.010
I felt bad for your poor eyebrows.
我为你的可怜眉毛感到难过。

627
00:25:52.010 --> 00:25:52.350
Yeah.
对。

628
00:25:52.390 --> 00:25:54.510
It was a real grease paint.
那是真正的油彩。

629
00:25:54.770 --> 00:25:55.810
They shellacked you.
他们给你喷了定型胶。

630
00:25:55.810 --> 00:25:56.270
Yeah.
对。

631
00:25:56.510 --> 00:25:59.490
I have a few little background catches for this cold open.
对于这个开场白，我有几个小小的背景花絮要分享。

632
00:25:59.710 --> 00:26:06.030
I want you guys to know that at 44 seconds, when Kevin is annoyed that Creed is such a good joker,
我想让你们知道，在44秒的时候，当凯文对克里德把小丑演得这么好感到恼火时，

633
00:26:06.270 --> 00:26:08.950
he brushes past me and knocks me over.
他从我身边擦身而过并把我撞倒了。

634
00:26:09.370 --> 00:26:13.670
This was like a little running bit Brian and I would have that if Kevin bumped into Angela,
这是我和布莱恩经常玩的一个小小的连贯桥段，如果凯文撞到安吉拉，

635
00:26:13.850 --> 00:26:14.530
she'd go flying.
她就会飞出去。

636
00:26:14.670 --> 00:26:17.590
It was like our own personal bit that cracked us up to no end.
这就像是我们俩的私人小笑料，把我们逗得乐不可支。

637
00:26:17.790 --> 00:26:22.410
When he did it, one of my cat ears fell forward and didn't come back up.
当他这么做的时候，我的一只猫耳朵往前倒了下去，再也没有弹起来。

638
00:26:22.410 --> 00:26:26.850
And I could feel it laying on top of my head and I was trying not to laugh.
我能感觉到它搭在我的头顶上，我当时正努力憋笑。

639
00:26:26.970 --> 00:26:30.290
And if you go to 44 seconds, you'll see that Angela's ear flops forward.
如果你去看44秒，你会看到安吉拉的耳朵向前耷拉着。

640
00:26:30.670 --> 00:26:36.090
I want you to know that three people that I reached out to on this episode pointed out that moment to me.
我想让你们知道，我为这一集联系的三个人都向我指出了那个时刻。

641
00:26:36.090 --> 00:26:36.650
I know.
我知道。

642
00:26:36.890 --> 00:26:37.490
I know.
我知道。

643
00:26:37.570 --> 00:26:38.950
They talked about it in the commentary too.
他们在评论音轨里也谈到了这一点。

644
00:26:39.170 --> 00:26:41.750
I think it's gone down in the lore of this episode.
我想这已经成为这一集传说的一部分了。

645
00:26:41.910 --> 00:26:42.330
I know.
我知道。

646
00:26:42.510 --> 00:26:48.470
And then the other thing was, you guys, they really let Ed as that cat play around and mess with John.
然后另一件事是，各位，他们真的让扮演那只猫的埃德四处走动并捉弄约翰。

647
00:26:48.470 --> 00:26:56.190
And in one take, Ed as Andy came up to Jim and rubbed on his leg, like kind of rubbed on him like a cat.
在其中一个镜头里，扮演安迪的埃德走到吉姆身边，蹭着他的腿，就像猫蹭人一样。

648
00:26:56.410 --> 00:26:58.330
And the two of them lost it.
他们两个人都笑崩了。

649
00:26:58.430 --> 00:27:01.130
It's in the bloopers, but they had a lot of fun with that.
这在NG花絮里，但他们拍得很开心。

650
00:27:01.250 --> 00:27:08.210
One of my favorite moments is when Andy, it says in the script, Andy walks back to his desk smugly.
我最喜欢的时刻之一就是安迪——剧本上写着，安迪洋洋得意地走回他的座位。

651
00:27:09.190 --> 00:27:13.190
And Ed's like sashay in that cat costume cracked me up.
艾德穿着那套猫咪服装扭腰摆臀的样子把我笑死。

652
00:27:13.610 --> 00:27:18.290
You guys know we love this fake elevator in our lobby, the Dunder Mifflin lobby.
你们知道我们大厅里这个假电梯，邓德米夫林大厅的假电梯，我们超爱。

653
00:27:18.650 --> 00:27:18.970
Yeah.
没错。

654
00:27:19.090 --> 00:27:19.790
We've talked about it.
我们聊过这个。

655
00:27:19.870 --> 00:27:21.590
Two wooden doors and a guy pulling a rope.
两扇木门，还有个拉绳子的伙计。

656
00:27:21.790 --> 00:27:21.990
Yep.
对。

657
00:27:22.170 --> 00:27:22.810
On the side.
在侧边。

658
00:27:22.990 --> 00:27:24.430
And they add all the sound effects later.
而且所有的音效都是事后加上去的。

659
00:27:24.690 --> 00:27:25.190
They add it all in.
全都是后期加的。

660
00:27:25.370 --> 00:27:31.830
Well, in the script, when Rain as Dwight arrives in the Joker outfit, he just was supposed to hop in the elevator.
好吧，按照剧本，当雷恩饰演的德怀特穿着小丑服到达时，他本来应该直接跳进电梯。

661
00:27:32.090 --> 00:27:36.110
And he was supposed to, a la the Joker, say, and here we go.
他本来应该像小丑一样说，我们上吧。

662
00:27:36.270 --> 00:27:37.510
And the doors would shut.
然后电梯门就会关上。

663
00:27:37.670 --> 00:27:37.910
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

664
00:27:38.110 --> 00:27:39.530
But it was just kind of falling flat.
但那个效果感觉有点平淡。

665
00:27:39.530 --> 00:27:43.250
So they came up with this alt about the magic trick of the pencil disappearing.
所以他们想出了这样一个备选方案，关于铅笔消失的魔术。

666
00:27:43.490 --> 00:27:45.550
And it wasn't really working still.
而且当时那样做还是觉得不太行。

667
00:27:45.770 --> 00:27:50.750
And so Anthony pitched, what if the doors close as he's saying the line?
于是安东尼提议，如果他在念台词的时候门就关上了呢？

668
00:27:51.050 --> 00:27:53.770
And then he opens them back up to finish the sentence.
然后他又把门重新拉开来把话说完。

669
00:27:54.090 --> 00:27:57.830
And they said they played around with this for a bit with the doors opening and closing,
他们说这个开门的桥段和关门的动作他们玩了好一会儿，

670
00:27:57.990 --> 00:28:02.530
which you and I know means that there was someone working that pulley really hard.
你我都清楚，这意味着有人在拼命拉那个滑轮。

671
00:28:02.730 --> 00:28:04.290
And that's how they found this moment.
他们就是这样找到这个精彩瞬间的。

672
00:28:04.290 --> 00:28:05.770
And I thought that was really fun.
我觉得这真的很有趣。

673
00:28:05.930 --> 00:28:06.830
That is awesome.
太棒了。

674
00:28:06.830 --> 00:28:11.170
Those things that happened on the fly like that in the moment, I love to hear about.
我特别喜欢听这种现场即兴发挥的事情。

675
00:28:11.490 --> 00:28:13.630
Now it's time to get into the episode.
现在是时候进入正片了。

676
00:28:13.830 --> 00:28:15.210
We're down in the warehouse.
我们来到了仓库。

677
00:28:15.210 --> 00:28:20.590
They are loading up a big truck so that they can take Holly to Nashua.
他们在装满一辆大卡车，好把霍莉送到纳舒厄去。

678
00:28:20.810 --> 00:28:21.250
Yes.
没错。

679
00:28:21.490 --> 00:28:23.130
We got a fan question.
我们收到一个粉丝提问。

680
00:28:23.390 --> 00:28:23.750
Okay.
好的。

681
00:28:24.150 --> 00:28:26.010
That is very funny to me.
这对我来说太搞笑了。

682
00:28:26.490 --> 00:28:27.110
Two people.
两个人。

683
00:28:27.350 --> 00:28:27.750
Okay.
好的。

684
00:28:36.830 --> 00:28:40.730
That this road trip started from the office rather than from her home.
这次公路旅行竟然是从办公室出发，而不是从她家里。

685
00:28:40.890 --> 00:28:43.610
This is such a good catch.
这个细节抓得太好了。

686
00:28:43.870 --> 00:28:47.030
Where did this stop coming from?
这个梗到底是从哪儿冒出来的？

687
00:28:47.950 --> 00:28:48.910
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

688
00:28:49.050 --> 00:28:52.610
I guess we have to justify it that they went to her apartment, packed it up.
我想我们得强行解释说，他们去了她公寓，把东西收拾好了。

689
00:28:52.670 --> 00:28:54.630
But then why did they drive to the warehouse?
但那他们为什么还要开车回仓库？

690
00:28:54.650 --> 00:28:56.070
Why not just leave?
为什么不直接出发？

691
00:28:56.820 --> 00:29:01.750
This piggybacks very nicely on a question that I had along with Aaron S.
这跟我和阿伦·S还有阿曼达·E共同的一个疑问完美契合。

692
00:29:01.890 --> 00:29:02.550
and Amanda E.
阿曼达·E。

693
00:29:02.770 --> 00:29:05.850
What is Holly wearing on the day she is moving?
霍莉在她搬家的那天穿的是什么？

694
00:29:06.070 --> 00:29:09.930
She is dressed in her work clothes, same as Pam driving to Pratt.
她穿的是工作服，就像开车去普拉特的帕姆一样。

695
00:29:09.990 --> 00:29:10.490
I know.
我知道。

696
00:29:10.810 --> 00:29:11.510
What is that?
那是怎么回事？

697
00:29:11.690 --> 00:29:12.870
Michael's more casual.
迈克尔穿得更休闲一些。

698
00:29:13.210 --> 00:29:16.030
He's got his little casual little like zippy jacket.
他穿着一件那种小小的休闲拉链夹克。

699
00:29:16.330 --> 00:29:16.590
Yes.
是的。

700
00:29:16.590 --> 00:29:22.070
Also, they pointed out, I don't think it looks like she had any intention of helping
另外，他们指出，我觉得她看起来根本没有要帮忙的意思

701
00:29:22.070 --> 00:29:23.610
move any of her own belongings.
搬走她自己的任何物品。

702
00:29:23.690 --> 00:29:25.370
She is not dressed for a move.
她的穿着根本不像是要搬家。

703
00:29:25.570 --> 00:29:26.070
No.
没有。

704
00:29:26.350 --> 00:29:27.050
She's not.
她确实没有。

705
00:29:27.330 --> 00:29:28.510
Why could she be casual?
她为什么能这么随性？

706
00:29:28.510 --> 00:29:29.230
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

707
00:29:29.410 --> 00:29:30.910
I thought these were good catches.
我觉得这些都是不错的发现。

708
00:29:31.270 --> 00:29:35.650
You know, I talked to Dave about this, and he said that during the prep for this episode,
你知道的，我跟戴夫聊过这个，他说在为这集做准备期间，

709
00:29:35.830 --> 00:29:43.490
they brought him a bunch of trucks to look at, and they were all giant 18-wheeler moving
他们拿来了一堆卡车让他看，全都是那种巨型十八轮搬家

710
00:29:43.490 --> 00:29:44.030
trucks.
大卡车。

711
00:29:44.030 --> 00:29:47.650
And he was like, how am I going to film with that?
当时他的反应是，我怎么用这玩意儿拍摄啊？

712
00:29:47.750 --> 00:29:48.810
How do I tow it?
我怎么拖动它？

713
00:29:49.010 --> 00:29:49.950
What am I doing?
我要干嘛？

714
00:29:50.410 --> 00:29:53.290
But he said he loves this truck that they found.
但他说他很喜欢他们找到的这辆卡车。

715
00:29:53.510 --> 00:29:54.550
It looked really realistic.
看起来真的很逼真。

716
00:29:54.550 --> 00:29:59.870
He also just loved that the back was open, because then when you got shots that, you
他也特别喜欢车厢后面是敞开的，因为这样当你拍到那些，

717
00:29:59.870 --> 00:30:04.670
know, the farther shots of them going down the road, it just like, you really felt the
你知道的，他们行驶在路上的远景镜头时，就会觉得，真的很像是在

718
00:30:04.670 --> 00:30:05.290
move.
搬家。

719
00:30:05.530 --> 00:30:05.790
Yeah.
对啊。

720
00:30:05.790 --> 00:30:07.190
Because you could see her bed.
因为你能看到她的床。

721
00:30:07.350 --> 00:30:08.370
You could see the stuff.
你能看到那些东西。

722
00:30:08.610 --> 00:30:08.810
Right.
没错。

723
00:30:08.910 --> 00:30:12.690
They said that they wanted the table hanging off the front, like in the bubble wrap.
他们说他们想让桌子挂在前面，就像用气泡膜包着那样。

724
00:30:12.870 --> 00:30:13.590
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

725
00:30:14.030 --> 00:30:14.490
I loved it, too.
我也很喜欢。

726
00:30:14.730 --> 00:30:15.630
Phil Props.
道具师菲尔。

727
00:30:15.750 --> 00:30:17.150
You know, we love Phil Props.
你知道的，我们都很喜欢道具师菲尔。

728
00:30:17.250 --> 00:30:22.110
He shared that Anthony and Dave really wanted Michael to have packed all kinds of crazy things
他分享说安东尼和戴夫其实很希望迈克尔为这次公路旅行

729
00:30:22.110 --> 00:30:22.830
for the road trip.
打包各种疯狂的东西。

730
00:30:23.010 --> 00:30:26.690
Like him and Holly are little kids, like the finger puppets and the cats in the cradle
就像他和霍莉是小孩子一样，比如手指木偶、翻绳游戏

731
00:30:26.690 --> 00:30:28.330
and the movies to watch.
还有要看的电影。

732
00:30:28.470 --> 00:30:31.050
You guys, a lot of those are in the deleted scenes.
伙计们，其中很多都在被删减片段里。

733
00:30:31.350 --> 00:30:31.710
Aw.
噢。

734
00:30:31.710 --> 00:30:33.770
Of them doing it in the van.
是他们在面包车里做这些事的片段。

735
00:30:34.030 --> 00:30:36.850
And my absolute favorite is the two of them.
我绝对最喜欢的一个镜头是他们两个。

736
00:30:36.990 --> 00:30:41.870
The windows are down, and they're watching a movie, and they are pissing themselves laughing.
车窗摇下来了，他们在看电影，笑得肚子都痛了。

737
00:30:42.050 --> 00:30:44.250
They are laughing so hard.
他们笑得太厉害了。

738
00:30:44.390 --> 00:30:45.690
And Daryl looks miserable.
而达里尔看起来痛苦极了。

739
00:30:45.950 --> 00:30:50.790
And Daryl takes a hard turn on purpose, and the laptop that's playing the movie goes flying
然后达里尔故意急转弯，正在播放电影的笔记本电脑就直接飞

740
00:30:50.790 --> 00:30:51.430
out the window.
出了窗外。

741
00:30:51.850 --> 00:30:53.390
I remember that.
我记得那个。

742
00:30:53.570 --> 00:30:54.710
It is so funny.
太搞笑了。

743
00:30:54.710 --> 00:30:56.590
I am so bummed it didn't make it in.
没能剪进正片里我真的好失落。

744
00:30:57.050 --> 00:31:01.790
Dave said they spent three hours on that gag and finally had to just let it go.
戴夫说他们在这个恶作剧上花了三个小时，最后只能放弃。

745
00:31:02.030 --> 00:31:06.430
They said every time Craig turned, the computer would slide and never go out the window.
他们说克雷格每次转弯，电脑都会滑掉，就是飞不出窗外。

746
00:31:06.490 --> 00:31:09.590
It only went out the window one time.
它就飞出去过一次。

747
00:31:10.090 --> 00:31:11.030
Oh, my gosh.
哦天哪。

748
00:31:11.030 --> 00:31:14.190
But it's in the bloopers on the DVD, and it's so funny.
但它在DVD的NG花絮里，真的超级搞笑。

749
00:31:14.490 --> 00:31:18.610
We had a fan catch from a couple of people, from Erica S.
我们收到了好几位粉丝的发现，来自埃里卡·S.

750
00:31:18.690 --> 00:31:20.930
and Mary S., and I have to say
和玛丽·S.，我必须说

751
00:31:20.930 --> 00:31:22.670
they're making a good point.
他们提出了一个很好的观点。

752
00:31:22.950 --> 00:31:23.430
What?
什么？

753
00:31:23.810 --> 00:31:31.330
So it's said repeatedly in Goodbye, Toby that, you know, she's coming in to train for this
所以在《再见，托比》中反复提到，你知道，她是来培训这个

754
00:31:31.330 --> 00:31:35.610
new position, and that they only allowed one day for training.
新岗位的，而且他们只给了一天的培训时间。

755
00:31:35.610 --> 00:31:41.270
And when she's on the Ferris wheel with Michael, she talks about how she was unable to be promoted
当她和迈克尔一起坐摩天轮时，她谈到自己如何在

756
00:31:41.270 --> 00:31:42.850
at her former company.
前公司无法获得晋升。

757
00:31:43.490 --> 00:31:44.430
Former company.
前公司。

758
00:31:44.530 --> 00:31:44.850
Right, right.
对，对。

759
00:31:45.030 --> 00:31:51.330
But then in this episode, it says she's being transferred back to Nashua, as if she's been
但在这集中，却说她被调回纳舒厄，就好像她

760
00:31:51.330 --> 00:31:53.350
a Dunder Mifflin employee all along.
一直都是邓德·米夫林的员工一样。

761
00:31:53.650 --> 00:31:54.890
I don't know, guys.
我不知道啊，伙计们。

762
00:31:55.090 --> 00:31:57.570
I mean, I think they caught a continuity error there.
我是说，我觉得他们那里抓到一个剧情连贯性错误。

763
00:31:57.750 --> 00:31:57.950
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

764
00:31:58.270 --> 00:32:00.290
Here's one of the things I was curious about.
这是我好奇的事情之一。

765
00:32:00.290 --> 00:32:06.850
Why would Daryl agree to drive Michael and Holly, be in a car with Michael and Holly
达里尔为什么会同意开车送迈克尔和霍莉，和迈克尔、霍莉

766
00:32:06.850 --> 00:32:08.010
for seven hours?
待在一辆车里七个小时？

767
00:32:08.570 --> 00:32:13.550
Well, there was a talking head in the script that didn't make it in that explained this.
嗯，剧本里有一个没播出的单采镜头解释了这一点。

768
00:32:13.770 --> 00:32:18.610
Daryl said, I'm driving them up for five times what I would have made at work.
达里尔说，我开车送他们上去，赚的钱是我上班五倍的工钱。

769
00:32:18.630 --> 00:32:20.150
I thought I made a good deal.
我以为我做了一笔好买卖。

770
00:32:20.430 --> 00:32:24.330
Then I realized I'm going to be trapped in a truck with Michael all day.
然后我才意识到我要一整天都被困在和迈克尔一起的卡车里。

771
00:32:24.710 --> 00:32:26.430
But he did earn a lot of money.
但他确实赚了很多钱。

772
00:32:26.690 --> 00:32:28.970
So Michael paid him is why.
所以是因为迈克尔付了他钱。

773
00:32:29.050 --> 00:32:29.910
They paid him, yeah.
他们付了他钱，对。

774
00:32:29.910 --> 00:32:32.450
Okay, that does make more sense.
好吧，这确实说得通了。

775
00:32:32.770 --> 00:32:35.250
Well, Michael is not the only person who's leaving for the day.
好了，迈克尔可不是唯一一个今天外出的人。

776
00:32:35.490 --> 00:32:36.930
Jim comes walking out of the building.
吉姆从大楼里走出来。

777
