00:38:59.790 --> 00:39:01.430
But they're driving Daryl crazy.
但他们把达里尔快折磨疯了。

943
00:39:01.430 --> 00:39:06.050
But then they start to realize this is far.
不过接着他们开始意识到这路程可真远。

944
00:39:06.990 --> 00:39:08.430
It's starting to hit them.
他们开始深有体会了。

945
00:39:08.930 --> 00:39:09.970
Michael wants to save the day.
迈克尔想要挺身而出拯救大家。

946
00:39:10.110 --> 00:39:11.290
He's like, stop right now.
他说，现在就停下。

947
00:39:11.550 --> 00:39:12.450
We're halfway.
我们已经走了一半了。

948
00:39:12.990 --> 00:39:15.910
There's got to be an amazing bed and breakfast right here.
这附近肯定有一家棒极了的家庭旅馆。

949
00:39:16.030 --> 00:39:17.230
Yeah, it's where we'll meet.
对，就是我们汇合的地方。

950
00:39:17.330 --> 00:39:18.010
It's going to be so cute.
一定会非常可爱。

951
00:39:18.010 --> 00:39:18.730
We'll meet in the middle.
我们在中间碰头。

952
00:39:19.090 --> 00:39:20.570
So they pull off the road.
所以他们把车开下了路。

953
00:39:21.050 --> 00:39:21.770
There is nothing.
结果什么也没有。

954
00:39:21.990 --> 00:39:22.790
They're in the woods.
他们身处树林中。

955
00:39:23.330 --> 00:39:26.190
Kyle, our location manager, shared this.
凯尔，我们的外景经理，分享了这件事。

956
00:39:26.630 --> 00:39:31.210
He said when they went tech scouting, they found this location kind of like off the side of the road.
他说他们去勘景时，发现了这个地方，有点像在路边。

957
00:39:31.370 --> 00:39:32.610
They were like, oh, this will be perfect.
他们当时觉得，哦，这太完美了。

958
00:39:33.110 --> 00:39:38.370
But then they found out another production was filming just a little ways down the way in the same area.
但后来他们发现，另一个剧组正在同一地区的同一条路不远处拍摄。

959
00:39:38.610 --> 00:39:38.790
Who was it?
是谁？

960
00:39:38.950 --> 00:39:40.450
He didn't say who it was.
他没说是谁。

961
00:39:40.550 --> 00:39:44.750
But he said normally this wouldn't concern us because we would film in our little nook.
但他说通常这不会影响我们，因为我们会在自己的小角落里拍。

962
00:39:44.830 --> 00:39:47.050
They would film in their nook and we'd be fine.
他们拍他们的角落，我们拍我们的，这就没问题。

963
00:39:47.170 --> 00:39:51.890
He said, but then we found out they were filming a live band all day.
他说，但后来我们发现他们一整天都在拍现场乐队演出。

964
00:39:51.890 --> 00:39:54.350
And he said, we couldn't have a live band.
他说，我们可受不了现场乐队的干扰。

965
00:39:54.350 --> 00:39:56.410
So we had to find a whole new location.
所以我们不得不重新找一个外景地。

966
00:39:56.630 --> 00:39:59.270
And this spot was actually in Griffith Park.
而这个地方其实是在格里芬公园。

967
00:39:59.730 --> 00:40:00.530
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

968
00:40:00.850 --> 00:40:01.010
Yeah.
是啊。

969
00:40:01.370 --> 00:40:04.050
It's so funny when you said another show was filming there.
你刚才说另一个剧组在那里拍摄的时候，我觉得真搞笑。

970
00:40:04.210 --> 00:40:08.610
I assumed it was like a murder show or 24 or something.
我以为会是什么谋杀悬疑剧或者《24小时》之类的情节。

971
00:40:08.850 --> 00:40:08.970
Right.
对啊。

972
00:40:09.250 --> 00:40:13.350
Because who else needs just like to be out in the weird woods?
因为还有谁需要跑到这种奇怪的树林里去？

973
00:40:13.450 --> 00:40:15.230
Maybe a teen rom-com.
也许是青春浪漫喜剧吧。

974
00:40:15.530 --> 00:40:17.350
I guess so with a live band.
带着现场乐队的青春片，我也只能这么想了。

975
00:40:17.550 --> 00:40:17.970
Right.
没错。

976
00:40:18.190 --> 00:40:20.150
Here's another little thing I caught, Jenna.
詹娜，我这里还抓到一个小细节。

977
00:40:20.150 --> 00:40:25.150
At 9 minutes, 53 seconds, while Michael and Holly are having this heart-to-heart in the car,
在第9分53秒，当迈克尔和霍莉在车里进行这场知心交谈时，

978
00:40:25.290 --> 00:40:26.270
Daryl's getting gas.
达里尔在加油。

979
00:40:26.530 --> 00:40:26.990
Right?
对吧？

980
00:40:27.310 --> 00:40:27.450
Yeah.
对。

981
00:40:27.870 --> 00:40:29.850
Did you see what the front license plate said?
你看到前车牌上写的是什么吗？

982
00:40:30.130 --> 00:40:30.610
No.
没有。

983
00:40:30.970 --> 00:40:33.230
It just says ROCK 107.
上面写着“ROCK 107”。

984
00:40:33.650 --> 00:40:35.550
The license plate on the truck?
卡车上的车牌？

985
00:40:35.690 --> 00:40:36.090
Yes.
对。

986
00:40:36.230 --> 00:40:38.830
On the front of the truck says ROCK 107.
卡车车头写着“ROCK 107”。

987
00:40:39.010 --> 00:40:39.530
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

988
00:40:39.530 --> 00:40:40.490
A radio station.
一家广播电台。

989
00:40:41.510 --> 00:40:44.310
Is there a ROCK 107 in Scranton?
斯克兰顿有“ROCK 107”电台吗？

990
00:40:44.490 --> 00:40:44.990
Yes.
有的。

991
00:40:45.250 --> 00:40:46.470
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

992
00:40:46.470 --> 00:40:47.990
It plays classic rock.
它播放经典摇滚乐。

993
00:40:48.230 --> 00:40:49.730
Of course it does, Sam.
当然啦，萨姆。

994
00:40:57.430 --> 00:40:58.470
ROCK 107.
ROCK 107。

995
00:40:58.730 --> 00:40:59.710
Yeah, baby.
耶，宝贝。

996
00:41:00.110 --> 00:41:05.630
Although I suppose, actually, these are all coming off of Michael's mix CD that he made for the trip.
不过我想，实际上，这些都是从迈克尔为这次旅行制作的混音CD里来的。

997
00:41:05.950 --> 00:41:07.030
Life is a Highway.
《生命是一条高速公路》。

998
00:41:07.810 --> 00:41:09.870
Now, we all know I made...
现在，我们都知道我做了……

999
00:41:09.870 --> 00:41:11.130
Your Scranton mix CD.
你的斯克兰顿混音CD。

1000
00:41:11.450 --> 00:41:12.110
Sounds of Scranton.
《斯克兰顿之声》。

1001
00:41:12.270 --> 00:41:15.810
I would have put this on there because it was just a mix of classic rock.
我本来会把这个放进去的，因为这只是一首经典摇滚串烧。

1002
00:41:15.990 --> 00:41:17.650
You know who would have appreciated my CD?
你知道谁会欣赏我的CD吗？

1003
00:41:18.130 --> 00:41:18.850
Michael Scott.
迈克尔·斯科特。

1004
00:41:18.970 --> 00:41:19.590
Michael Scott.
迈克尔·斯科特。

1005
00:41:19.790 --> 00:41:21.410
Jenna Fisher and Michael Scott.
珍娜·费舍尔和迈克尔·斯科特。

1006
00:41:21.510 --> 00:41:21.790
Yes.
是的。

1007
00:41:21.790 --> 00:41:22.470
Hanging out.
闲逛。

1008
00:41:22.650 --> 00:41:32.510
So, while Daryl is getting gas, you know, Michael says that he's dated four women in the last 10 years, and Holly surpasses them all.
所以，趁达里尔去加油的时候，迈克尔说他在过去10年里约会过四个女人，而霍莉超过了她们所有人。

1009
00:41:32.990 --> 00:41:37.070
Well, Veda, our script, he shared that the last 10 years was an improv from Steve.
对啊，维达，我们的剧本，他透露说过去10年的事是史蒂夫即兴发挥的。

1010
00:41:37.370 --> 00:41:41.050
Oh, it made it so much better, I have to say.
哦，这让效果好太多了，我得这么说。

1011
00:41:41.450 --> 00:41:41.530
I know.
我知道。

1012
00:41:41.530 --> 00:41:41.910
I know.
我知道。

1013
00:41:41.910 --> 00:41:50.310
So, everything about that when she thinks he means four people in the last year, and he says in the last 10 years, kind of at the same time.
所以，当她以为他指的是过去一年里的四个人，而他说的是过去10年里，那种几乎同时发生的一切。

1014
00:41:50.530 --> 00:41:50.710
Yeah.
对。

1015
00:41:50.750 --> 00:41:52.310
I was like, oh, Michael.
当时我就想，哦，迈克尔。

1016
00:41:52.470 --> 00:41:52.850
I know.
我知道。

1017
00:41:52.970 --> 00:41:54.370
I love you so much, Michael.
我太爱你了，迈克尔。

1018
00:41:54.530 --> 00:41:56.050
And they were ad-libbing right there.
而且他们当时就在那里即兴表演。

1019
00:41:56.290 --> 00:41:56.730
Aw.
噢。

1020
00:41:57.330 --> 00:42:04.310
All of it really breaks my heart, Ange, because as they're getting closer, you can really see Holly shutting down.
所有这些真的让我心碎，安吉，因为随着他们越来越亲近，你真的能看到霍莉在自我封闭。

1021
00:42:04.310 --> 00:42:07.110
Oh, she starts crying while the song is playing.
哦，背景音乐放着的时候，她就开始哭了。

1022
00:42:07.130 --> 00:42:07.470
I know.
我知道。

1023
00:42:07.470 --> 00:42:09.430
And Amy Ryan crushed that.
艾米·莱恩这段演得太棒了。

1024
00:42:09.590 --> 00:42:09.990
I know.
我知道。

1025
00:42:10.090 --> 00:42:11.250
That was so good.
太精彩了。

1026
00:42:11.570 --> 00:42:12.630
Well, Dave talked about this.
对，戴夫谈到了这一点。

1027
00:42:12.690 --> 00:42:15.470
He said, you know, he really wanted a three shot.
他说，你知道的，他真的很想要一个三人同框镜头。

1028
00:42:15.750 --> 00:42:19.310
He wanted to see Michael and Holly having this moment.
他想看到迈克尔和霍莉度过这个时刻。

1029
00:42:19.490 --> 00:42:21.570
Michael begging Holly, no, don't do this.
迈克尔哀求霍莉，不，别这样。

1030
00:42:21.630 --> 00:42:22.550
We don't need to break up.
我们不需要分手。

1031
00:42:22.710 --> 00:42:24.950
And Daryl just making a random phone call.
而达里尔只是在随便打个电话。

1032
00:42:25.090 --> 00:42:26.770
Like, does he need to talk to anyone, someone?
就好像，他非得跟什么人、某个人说话吗？

1033
00:42:27.130 --> 00:42:27.270
Yes.
是的。

1034
00:42:27.270 --> 00:42:29.730
And he wanted to see all of that at the same time.
他想同时看到这一切。

1035
00:42:29.950 --> 00:42:32.670
I mean, it's not an easy shot, but Dave was like, no, no, no.
我的意思是，这并不是一个简单的镜头，但戴夫态度坚决，不，不，不。

1036
00:42:32.750 --> 00:42:34.770
I want to see all three of them.
我想同时看到他们三个。

1037
00:42:34.990 --> 00:42:36.410
You had to see all three of them.
你必须同时看到他们三个。

1038
00:42:36.410 --> 00:42:36.550
Yeah.
对。

1039
00:42:36.850 --> 00:42:38.110
It only works that way.
只有这样才行得通。

1040
00:42:38.210 --> 00:42:41.050
Because he said it's like two scenes happening at the same time.
因为他说这就像两个场景同时在发生。

1041
00:42:41.370 --> 00:42:45.910
Well, maybe we should take a break from the car, because we need to cover what's happening back at the office.
好吧，也许我们该从车里的情景暂停一下，因为我们需要聊聊办公室里发生的事情。

1042
00:42:46.290 --> 00:42:46.790
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1043
00:42:46.990 --> 00:42:48.810
Dwight is applying for Cornell, you guys.
迪 Dwight 正在申请康奈尔大学，伙计们。

1044
00:42:49.190 --> 00:42:49.750
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1045
00:42:50.130 --> 00:42:52.430
And also, Pam's about to have lunch with Jim's brothers.
还有，帕姆快要和吉姆的兄弟们吃午饭了。

1046
00:42:52.550 --> 00:42:54.010
There's a lot to still talk about.
还有很多事情要谈。

1047
00:42:54.390 --> 00:42:55.330
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

1048
00:43:05.700 --> 00:43:07.960
Dwight arrives to work.
迪 Dwight 到达公司。

1049
00:43:08.200 --> 00:43:08.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1050
00:43:08.760 --> 00:43:11.060
He is wearing a Cornell sweatshirt.
他穿着一件康奈尔大学的卫衣。

1051
00:43:11.240 --> 00:43:13.060
Over his mustard shirt.
套在他的芥末黄色衬衫外面。

1052
00:43:13.360 --> 00:43:13.960
Yeah.
对。

1053
00:43:14.340 --> 00:43:16.020
You want to know why he's wearing that sweatshirt?
你想知道他为什么穿着那件运动衫吗？

1054
00:43:16.200 --> 00:43:18.000
Because he's applying to Cornell.
因为他在申请康奈尔大学。

1055
00:43:18.300 --> 00:43:18.920
That's right.
没错。

1056
00:43:19.120 --> 00:43:19.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1057
00:43:19.720 --> 00:43:20.160
Yes.
是的。

1058
00:43:20.420 --> 00:43:23.900
I mean, did he know how to go after Andy or what?
我是说，他知道怎么去针对安迪，对吧？

1059
00:43:24.080 --> 00:43:24.440
Oh.
哦。

1060
00:43:24.660 --> 00:43:28.300
What does Andy covet that Cornell diploma?
安迪有多渴望那张康奈尔的文凭？

1061
00:43:28.700 --> 00:43:34.700
My favorite thing is when you see Andy fuming in the back of Dwight's talking head.
我最喜欢的一幕是，你看到安迪在德怀特的单人访谈背景里气得冒烟。

1062
00:43:34.700 --> 00:43:34.840
Through the window.
透过窗户。

1063
00:43:34.840 --> 00:43:36.840
When he's bobbing his chair back and forth.
当他把椅子前后晃动的时候。

1064
00:43:37.060 --> 00:43:37.780
So good.
太棒了。

1065
00:43:37.920 --> 00:43:38.440
So good.
太棒了。

1066
00:43:38.620 --> 00:43:42.160
I have a little Phil Props tidbit about this talking head.
关于这个单人访谈，我有一个关于道具师菲尔的小花絮。

1067
00:43:42.540 --> 00:43:45.960
Dwight is holding up a coffee mug that also says Cornell.
德怀特举着一个同样写着康奈尔字样的咖啡杯。

1068
00:43:46.240 --> 00:43:46.380
Yeah.
对。

1069
00:43:46.560 --> 00:43:48.940
Well, this was sort of a last-minute pitch from Dave.
这个嘛，这是戴夫临时提出的一个想法。

1070
00:43:48.940 --> 00:43:51.440
He really wanted to pump up the Cornell merch.
他真的很想大力推销康奈尔的周边商品。

1071
00:43:51.620 --> 00:43:51.840
Okay.
好吧。

1072
00:43:51.840 --> 00:43:54.260
So he was like, what if he's holding something?
所以他就提议，如果他手里拿点东西会怎么样？

1073
00:43:54.500 --> 00:43:57.420
They made that mug in two hours.
他们两个小时内就做出了那个杯子。

1074
00:43:57.540 --> 00:43:57.940
What?
什么？

1075
00:43:58.160 --> 00:43:59.080
Our props department.
我们的道具部门。

1076
00:43:59.420 --> 00:44:00.420
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1077
00:44:00.580 --> 00:44:00.740
Yeah.
对。

1078
00:44:00.900 --> 00:44:03.160
So that he could have it in this talking head.
这样他就能在这个单人访谈里拿着用。

1079
00:44:03.420 --> 00:44:08.440
You know, I've seen that happen on set sometimes where there'll be an actor and they're supposed
你知道，我有几次在片场看到过这种情况，比如有个演员，他们本该

1080
00:44:08.440 --> 00:44:09.820
to carry a briefcase.
拎着一个公文包。

1081
00:44:09.940 --> 00:44:10.080
Yeah.
对。

1082
00:44:10.200 --> 00:44:10.680
For example.
举个例子。

1083
00:44:10.980 --> 00:44:14.520
And the props team will come up during the rehearsal of the scene.
然后道具团队会在场景排练期间过来。

1084
00:44:14.520 --> 00:44:19.940
Then on the day, we're lighting, we're getting ready to shoot, and they show the actor three
接着到了拍摄当天，我们在打光，准备开拍，他们向演员展示了三个

1085
00:44:19.940 --> 00:44:21.340
briefcase options.
公文包选项。

1086
00:44:21.540 --> 00:44:21.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1087
00:44:21.980 --> 00:44:25.000
And then the actor says, oh, no, no.
然后演员说，哦，不，不。

1088
00:44:25.060 --> 00:44:28.240
I imagined it would be like a distressed leather.
我脑补的是那种做旧皮革质感的。

1089
00:44:28.520 --> 00:44:31.760
Maybe it was my father's that they passed down to me.
也许是我父亲传给我的那种。

1090
00:44:32.140 --> 00:44:37.240
And the props person, you just see them just having a heart attack, basically.
然后道具人员，你就能看到他们简直快要心脏病发作了。

1091
00:44:37.240 --> 00:44:42.040
And I feel like the actor and director's producers, the writer of the episode, they might all have
我觉得演员、导演、制片人、这一集的编剧，他们可能都会像这样

1092
00:44:42.040 --> 00:44:44.060
a thought last minute like that.
在最后一刻冒出一个想法。

1093
00:44:44.160 --> 00:44:46.220
On what this prop should look like.
关于这个道具应该长什么样。

1094
00:44:46.520 --> 00:44:51.280
And the props person is like, always, without fail, they're always like, oh, yeah, yeah,
而道具人员总是，毫无例外地，总是说，哦，行，行，

1095
00:44:51.460 --> 00:44:51.660
okay.
好吧。

1096
00:44:52.020 --> 00:44:52.640
No problem.
没问题。

1097
00:44:53.000 --> 00:44:53.720
We'll get that.
我们去弄。

1098
00:44:53.880 --> 00:45:00.040
And then I know that they take like a van to some warehouse and they go through a giant
然后我知道他们会开着面包车去某个仓库，在堆满所有这些公文包的巨大

1099
00:45:00.040 --> 00:45:04.580
shelf of all these briefcases to try to find the thing that the actor talked about.
货架上翻找，试图找到演员刚才说的那种东西。

1100
00:45:04.960 --> 00:45:07.020
Or they run across the parking lot.
或者他们直接冲过停车场。

1101
00:45:07.020 --> 00:45:07.320
Yeah.
对。

1102
00:45:07.760 --> 00:45:10.420
And like try to get something printed in the moment.
然后就想立刻打印点什么出来。

1103
00:45:10.820 --> 00:45:14.980
I have such a memory of Phil running across the parking lot.
我太记得菲尔在停车场奔跑的画面了。

1104
00:45:15.040 --> 00:45:15.360
Multiple times.
